                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "70a01099-6041-3203-8789-b976147183e8",
                        "entry_id": "9f676f22-fb8b-3a6a-a494-b304f1918f9a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To walk or move with a bouncing or undulating motion and at an unhurried pace."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ec5b07f-35d1-4577-8868-24d484fc6f1a",
                                "sense_id": "70a01099-6041-3203-8789-b976147183e8",
                                "text": "Every available spyglass was directed towards this strange sail. It appeared, as we all watched it, to lollop up and down, as it were, with the jerk of the sea, according to no regular motion of a ship or boat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f988269a-b712-4406-ab6a-4e8146e50012",
                                "sense_id": "70a01099-6041-3203-8789-b976147183e8",
                                "text": "And the Camel said ‘Humph!’ again; but no sooner had he said it than he saw his back, that he was so proud of, puffing up and puffing up into a great big lolloping humph."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7093a13b-8084-4e75-ac61-9e43a4bcccf5",
                                "sense_id": "70a01099-6041-3203-8789-b976147183e8",
                                "text": "The carts rattle by, swinging from side to side; two Chinamen lollop along under their wooden yokes with the straining vegetable baskets—their pigtails and blue blouses fly out in the wind."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "448e0e10-9db2-48d1-83fb-645b98ad1e80",
                                "sense_id": "70a01099-6041-3203-8789-b976147183e8",
                                "text": "With a timid, loutish movement the great beast turned aside, then lumbered off followed by the calf. The other buffalo also extricated itself from the slime and lolloped away."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd2ed371-687d-4a09-af96-d0907a6014a4",
                                "sense_id": "70a01099-6041-3203-8789-b976147183e8",
                                "text": "And first they saw the red through the trees, and then the whole coach. And no wonder it was so long coming, the horses were only just lolloping along; because it wasn't the coach that carried the mails."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "01963061-6a24-4883-805c-a1b61cefbcfd",
                                "sense_id": "70a01099-6041-3203-8789-b976147183e8",
                                "text": "Collecting the ball midway inside his own half, the lolloping Togolese striker exploited generosity in the home defence by ambling downfield and then shaped a sumptuous shot into the top-right corner from 25 yards."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c188bb6-aa34-480b-9a93-18778ccd9d13",
                                "sense_id": "70a01099-6041-3203-8789-b976147183e8",
                                "text": "After a flamboyant snare drum roll intro, the catchy plinky-plonky piano melody is joined by lolloping xylophone and flutes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cf5aacde-f6d9-3d6f-ac53-b113c79a923b",
                        "entry_id": "9f676f22-fb8b-3a6a-a494-b304f1918f9a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To act lazily, loll, lie around."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f22f387a-b414-4e08-929c-b5b313b54f94",
                                "sense_id": "cf5aacde-f6d9-3d6f-ac53-b113c79a923b",
                                "text": "“Here’s fine discipline on-board, when such lazy, skulking sons of bitches as you are allowed, on pretence of sickness, to lollop at your ease, while your betters are kept to hard duty!”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a95d2ef-c4f9-4433-84e5-f623b95474f1",
                                "sense_id": "cf5aacde-f6d9-3d6f-ac53-b113c79a923b",
                                "text": "Mr. Meadows, who was seated in the middle of the box, was lolloping upon the table with his customary ease, and picking his teeth with his usual inattention to all about him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9263de5-2a1c-4b07-9e57-7bc23ed57c48",
                                "sense_id": "cf5aacde-f6d9-3d6f-ac53-b113c79a923b",
                                "text": "“Your uncle is, and always will be, a dull calculator, Nell,” observed the mother, after a long pause in a conversation that had turned on the labours of the day; “a lazy hand at figures and foreknowledge is that said Ishmael Bush! Here he sat lolloping about the rock from light till noon, doing nothing but scheme—scheme—scheme— […]”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
